```

This is permitted because Tiger is covariant with Animal.

Answer: ```java
class Animal {
}
class Tiger extends Animal {
}
class Demo {
public Animal display() {
Animal animal = new Animal();
return animal;
}
}
class Demo1 extends Demo {
public Tiger display() {
Tiger t = new Tiger();
return t;
}
}
```

Here, Demo1 overrides display() from Demo. The parent method returns Animal, while the child method returns Tiger. Since Tiger extends Animal, the return types are covariant.
